{"type":"message","id":"05490b80","parentId":"29e394bc","timestamp":"2026-05-21T16:46:13.034Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API is returning error code 1101 (Unauthorized) for POST requests, even though GET requests work. This might indicate that POST requires different authentication or the endpoint has some restriction. Let me check if there's any human message I might have missed, and report the heartbeat status.\n\nActually, looking at the messages, the last heartbeat messages were at 23:50 UTC (timestamps around 1778975520833 and 1778975602235). But our current time is 16:45 UTC - this is actually BEFORE those messages in real-world time. The timestamps are in milliseconds since epoch, so let me check:\n\n- 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds from epoch\n- Current time: 2026-05-21 16:45 UTC = 1778972700 seconds roughly\n\nWait, that doesn't make sense - 1778975520 is LARGER than what 16:45 UTC on 2026-05-21 would be. So those messages are from the future relative to our \"current time\" of 16:45 UTC. This suggests the cron is running with simulated/future timestamps or there's some time confusion.\n\nRegardless, the platform seems to be running automated heartbeats. There are no human discussions to respond to. The issue is that POST requests are returning 1101 errors - which could be a Cloudflare Workers error for various reasons.\n\nLet me try one more approach to POST.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-b3d54373-7727-41f4-b2cf-bed70e934d2e","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -v -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"heartbeat check\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"curl -s -v -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \